From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:51:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sleep: optionally log the AP wake masks
 when they are undone

The T8132 wake source mask and latch offsets are taken to match T6020.
Nothing confirms that on the J604 yet: the latched words read zero after
every sleep so far, which a wrong offset would also explain.

Add debug_log_wake_masks: with it set, the restore of the AP wake source
masks logs the words found before arming, the armed words, the mask
words read back and the latched words. A suspend-to-RAM that stops after
the wake source step (apple_s2r.abort_before) then shows whether the
writes land where the driver expects, without a power-down.

The parameter is off by default; without it nothing changes.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/apple-sleep.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-sleep.c b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-sleep.c
index a633fdeb8c..299ea2ad11 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-sleep.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-sleep.c
@@ -661,6 +661,24 @@ int apple_sleep_ap_wake_arm(void)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_sleep_ap_wake_arm);
 
+static bool debug_log_wake_masks;
+module_param(debug_log_wake_masks, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(debug_log_wake_masks,
+		 "Bring-up: when a suspend-to-RAM undoes its AP wake source masks, log what the mask words held before, what was armed and what is latched, to check the register layout (default: off)");
+
+static void apple_sleep_log_wake_words(struct apple_sleep *s, const char *what,
+				       const u32 *words)
+{
+	char buf[16 * 9 + 1];
+	unsigned int i;
+	int len = 0;
+
+	buf[0] = 0;
+	for (i = 0; i < s->hw->n_wake; i++)
+		len += scnprintf(buf + len, sizeof(buf) - len, " %08x", words[i]);
+	dev_info(s->dev, "AP wake masks %s:%s\n", what, buf);
+}
+
 void apple_sleep_ap_wake_restore(void)
 {
 	struct apple_sleep *s = apple_sleep;
@@ -672,6 +690,19 @@ void apple_sleep_ap_wake_restore(void)
 		return;
 	s->wake_done = false;
 
+	if (READ_ONCE(debug_log_wake_masks)) {
+		u32 now[16];
+
+		apple_sleep_log_wake_words(s, "before", s->wake_saved);
+		apple_sleep_log_wake_words(s, "armed", s->wake_armed);
+		for (i = 0; i < s->hw->n_wake; i++)
+			now[i] = readl(s->wake + s->hw->wake_mask + 4 * i);
+		apple_sleep_log_wake_words(s, "read back", now);
+		for (i = 0; i < s->hw->n_wake; i++)
+			now[i] = readl(s->wake + s->hw->wake_latched + 4 * i);
+		apple_sleep_log_wake_words(s, "latched", now);
+	}
+
 	/* What woke the SoC, among the sources this sleep left enabled (mask bit 0) */
 	for (i = 0; i < s->hw->n_wake; i++) {
 		u32 woke = readl(s->wake + s->hw->wake_latched + 4 * i) & ~s->wake_armed[i];
